:: Codex Brother 2 [codex char-Brother2 todo] {"position":"2260,1370","size":"100,100"}
!Brother 2
''Where:'' District 4: Suburbia
''Appears in:'' [[Act 3|A3 Brother 2]]
<<if $trust["Brother 2"] isnot undefined>>''Trust:'' <<print $trust["Brother 2"]>><</if>>
''Description:'' NPC - spiky, cantankerous, absent-minded
''Age:'' 75
''Gender:'' Male (he/him)
''Origin:'' Underwater Creature
''Occupation:'' Mechanic
''Faction:'' Long-standing member of the mechanics guild


''Physical Description:'' 

Abol is a crusty, stringy, lanky old man, made crooked by years of chin-stroking and head-scratching. He is the identical twin of Willun, with whom he is bound together, side by side, so that Abol is the left hand-side of the chimera.


''Overview'' 

Abol is one of the co-founders of Willun & Abol Quality Mechanics Ltd, alongside his brother Willun. Founded many decades ago, in their youth, the brothers are quality mechanics that have moved with the times and mastered fixing up all kinds of tech. Abol in his day was a crafty technician, taking on fiddly, technical jobs with grace and ingenuity.

However, the tides of time and familiarity have turned the brothers bitter towards each other, and they have fallen into constant bickering and moaning. A few days before Player arrives, Aishui enacted a mischievous plan to get the brothers working together again: binding them together, side-by-side using a coral/seaweed bind. However, this only intensified the bickering and arguing, and worse: the two old identical siblings have now forgotten which one is which. This presents an argument so intense that they simply refuse to work until it has been resolved.


''Relationships''

''Abol'' - Abol’s brother of 75 years, a fast and relentless partner who complemented Abol’s technical work. Sadly, years of working together has turned the brothers bitter and their current relationship consists mainly of bickering, heckling and name-calling.

''Aishui'' - Willun and Abol are familiars of Aishui as he passes through the neighbourhood from time to time. Currently they are both very pissed off at having been bound together on account of Aishui’s mischievous scheme.

''Sabelle'' - Abol discovered Sabelle secretly using the brothers’ workshop a few years ago, as they had been forbidden from practicing invention due to their age and social status. Abol saw the talent that Sabelle possesses and agreed to turn a blind eye to them using the brothers’ workshop whenever they needed. The brothers are both currently a little hurt that Sabelle has conspired with Aisgui to bind them together.


''Connections''

''Mechanics' Guild'' - Both brothers are longtime members of the mechanics guild, licensed to work on all forms of technology.


''World Knowledge''

Abol was always the brains behind the company. He has a great textbook knowledge of the technology that has developed in the wider ocean, and a slightly broader horizon than his brother. He can explain things very well, and has more sensitivity to the other folk of the Atlantis, who often visit when they need things fixed. His knowledge is currently hindered by the fact he doesn’t currently know which brother he is.


''Goal and Obstacle''

Abol needs to remember which brother he is before the pair can start working again. The problem is, due to the brothers’ bickering nature, it makes it impossible to discern.

The Player must find out information about the brothers’ characters from other characters in the district. However, whenever information is relayed to the brothers, they both want to identify with the character who is being described. Ultimately the Player must find out a certain dish which Willun loves but Abol is repulsed by, and deliver it to them to provoke their natural reactions, and make them remember who they are. Once that is resolved, they are willing and able to use their complementary skills once more to fix up the manta-ray ornithopter.


''Initial perception of the Player Character''

Both brothers are too invested in bickering to really pay too much attention to the MC initially. Once the quest is complete, Abol becomes trusting of the Player and happy to work out how to fix the ornithopter.


''Vocal Profile:'' Abol has a creaky, old vocal delivery, higher-pitched than low. He is spiky and snappy when he gets annoyed.

''Speech Patterns:'' He is blunt and abrupt with his words when fighting and arguing. Once he remembers that he is Abol, he is more rambling and excitable in speech profile.



